# Held to the versions in requirements-windows-cu128.lock.txt. A fresh Linux resolve
# picks newer ones, and a pool where a Linux worker and a Windows worker run
# different versions can return two different answers to the same job spec without
# announcing it. `ultralytics-platform` is the one that matters -- it is in the
# inference path, and VP1 has already drifted to 0.1.48 against a lock saying 0.1.40.
# The rest are pinned for reproducibility rather than because they are known to
# affect detections.
ultralytics-platform==0.1.40
filelock==3.32.6
fsspec==2026.7.0
idna==3.19
urllib3==2.7.0

# torch is pinned to 2.11.0 rather than the newest available, because 2.11.0 is the
# newest version present on BOTH cu126 and cu128. Pinning each variant to its own
# maximum put three torch versions in a four-machine pool answering the same job
# specs -- 2.14.0 on two boxes and 2.11.0 on the Blackwell laptop, with nothing
# announcing the difference. One version across every variant is worth more than a
# newer one on some of them.
